: "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01EBmSEBkZJv7hKtK5rudEme", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PWt1aG4xLmgVkAhGi4nH7A", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019E3mwpcENCAp6yBBiax89a", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BgF9vmB2DXSRiG7Rb4xQid", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013pUZkkkAHyd2u4TMrQ5ZHp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "`round_money` in `src/money.py` was documented as using banker's rounding (FIN-212) but actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, causing `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build.\n\nThis switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (e.g. 2.665 -> 2.66, 2.675 -> 2.68).\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch. CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` says it uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. Under that mode, 2.665 rounds to 2.67, while the test expects 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed the import and the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Now 2.665 rounds to 2.66 and 2.675 to 2.68, as the test expects. That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 on commit `08d3cd5986` passed.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory tool didn't recognize that ID. The fix follows the function's own description and the test.\n\nI haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}